## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/feather.html
- Summary (EN): The Feather node reduces abrupt contrast changes by capping how quickly values can change from one pixel to the next. This gives height fields a beveled appearance, and it can extend masks outward or inward without blurring them the way the Blur COP does.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Feather limite la vitesse de variation d'une valeur d'un pixel à l'autre, ce qui biseaute un champ de hauteur sans le flouter.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer to feather", "mask: optional per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: how much of the new value is mixed with the original; default 1 uses only the new value", "Feather from High to Low: when on, bright pixels stay and darker neighbors are raised; when off, dark pixels stay and bright pixels are lowered", "Include Border: samples initial pixel values from outside the image bounds, which can create an edge mask from constant borders", "Feather Direction: Diamond, Square, Octagon, Custom (uses Sweep Directions), or Circle", "Sweep Directions: Custom only; selects which of the eight directions apply, allowing one-sided ramp-like feathers", "Feather Method: Distance for Unit Change (distance over which a value of 1 changes to 0) or Change per Distance; the two are inverses"]

- Caveats: ["To create a tiling texture, turn on Include Border, and the feather may need to be repeated twice"]

